==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|tanstaafl}}
* {{l|en|TINSTAAFL|gloss=there is no such thing as a free lunch}}

===Etymology===
Acronym, originating in the early 20th century, and popularized by {{w|Robert A. Heinlein|Robert Heinlein's}} novel ''{{w|The Moon Is a Harsh Mistress}}''.

===Phrase===
{{en-phrase}}

# {{acronym of|en|there ain't no such thing as a free lunch|nodot=1}}; something advertised as being "free" will invariably have hidden costs.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1966|author={{w|Robert Heinlein}}|title={{w|The Moon Is A Harsh Mistress}}|passage="Gospodin," he said presently, "you used an odd word earlier--odd to me, I mean..."<br />"Oh, ''''tanstaafl'''.' Means 'There ain't no such thing as a free lunch.' And isn't," I added, pointing to a FREE LUNCH sign across room, "or these drinks would cost half as much. Was reminding her that anything free costs twice as much in long run or turns out worthless."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1985|author={{w|Lance Parkin}}|title=The Infinity Doctors|page=229|passage=''''Tanstaafl'''. There ain't no such thing as a free lunch. We both know that I was brought here for a reason. If we could get down to business.'}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1985|title=Economic Statecraft|chapter=National Power and Economic Statecraft|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=1tgP1Zi7kwwC&pg=PA140|first=David Allen|last=Baldwin|isbn=9780691101750|page=140|passage=The '''TANSTAAFL''' principle applies to all techniques of statecraft, not just the economic ones.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|title=Sound System Design and Optimization|chapter=Calibration|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=tFf__BD16EcC&pg=PT440|first=Bob|last=McCarthy|isbn=9781136123900|page=433|passage=The '''TANSTAAFL''' principle will come into play with each implementation of a calibration setting. There are no effects without side-effects. An improvement at one location will change others.}}

